# A minimal, hand-written portal frame: a flat rectangular border with a
# rectangular hole in the middle, defining a genuine opening to look
# through. ViroPortal requires an actual 3D model to define its shape (no
# built-in default frame) — we don't have the original prototype's door
# model, and OBJ is a simple enough plain-text format to write by hand
# rather than needing to source/license an external asset.
#
# Outer rectangle: 2m wide x 2.5m tall. Inner (hole): 1.6m x 2m.
# All vertices sit at Z=0 (flat), normals face +Z (toward the camera).

# Outer corners
v -1.0 -1.25 0.0
v  1.0 -1.25 0.0
v  1.0  1.25 0.0
v -1.0  1.25 0.0
# Inner corners (the hole)
v -0.8 -1.0 0.0
v  0.8 -1.0 0.0
v  0.8  1.0 0.0
v -0.8  1.0 0.0

vn 0.0 0.0 1.0

# Bottom edge of the frame
f 1//1 2//1 6//1
f 1//1 6//1 5//1
# Right edge
f 2//1 3//1 7//1
f 2//1 7//1 6//1
# Top edge
f 3//1 4//1 8//1
f 3//1 8//1 7//1
# Left edge
f 4//1 1//1 5//1
f 4//1 5//1 8//1
